{"name":"Caps","hex":"#7e7a75","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Caps","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of Cap"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Caps"}],"entries":[{"title":"GCHQ","blocks":[{"text":"Government Communications Headquarters (GCHQ) is an intelligence and security organisation responsible for providing signals intelligence (SIGINT) and information assurance (IA) to the government and the armed forces of the United Kingdom. Primarily based at The Doughnut in the suburbs of Cheltenham, GCHQ is the responsibility of the country's Secretary of State for Foreign and Commonwealth Affairs, but it is not a part of the Foreign Office and its director ranks as a Permanent Secretary."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/GCHQ-aerial.jpg/330px-GCHQ-aerial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GCHQ"},{"title":"Java Caps","blocks":[{"text":"Java Composite Application Platform Suite (Java CAPS) is a standards-based enterprise service bus software suite from Oracle Corporation. The suite has several components that help to integrate existing applications and deliver new business services in a service-oriented architecture environment. It is a Java EE compliant platform and provides application-to-application integration, business-to-business integration, business process management along with integrated human workflow, an Enterprise Information Portal, extract transform and load (ETL), business activity monitoring and composite application development."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Java_Caps"},{"title":"Caps (gamer)","blocks":[{"text":"Rasmus Borregaard Winther, better known by his in-game name Caps, is a Danish professional League of Legends player for G2 Esports. Widely regarded as the greatest Western League of Legends players of all time, he has spent most of his career with G2, where he has become the team's franchise player."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Caps_2025.jpg/330px-Caps_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caps_(gamer)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Allidina-Visram.jpg/500px-Allidina-Visram.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Allidina-Visram.jpg/1280px-Allidina-Visram.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Allidina-Visram.jpg/500px-Allidina-Visram.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Allidina Visram school in Mombasa, pictured above in 2006, was the location of the British \"Kilindini\" codebreaking outpost during World War II.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAllidina-Visram.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/NUCPS_banner.jpg/500px-NUCPS_banner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/NUCPS_banner.jpg/1280px-NUCPS_banner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/NUCPS_banner.jpg/500px-NUCPS_banner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"NUCPS banner on march in Cheltenham 1992","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANUCPS_banner.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Java_Caps_Netbeans_Console.png/120px-Java_Caps_Netbeans_Console.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Java_Caps_Netbeans_Console.png/250px-Java_Caps_Netbeans